JABBERWOCK'S NEXT 3 PROPOSED REFACTORS
==============================================================================

  1. EXTEND THE CONCEPT WALKER WITH PATTERN: "X when Y (conditional)"
     rationale: 177 walker-missed concepts match this pattern. Adding a single parser stanza to domains/concept_promotion_rules.py would lift them all to Term-tree definitions in one pass.
     files: domains/concept_promotion_rules.py (add parse_<pattern_name>() + emit_<pattern_name>_term() alongside parse_equation_identity)

  2. WIRE INTRA-Mt HOLDS REFERENCES IN: engineering
     rationale: 10 Mts have >=10 concepts AND no concept Holds-references any sibling. They read as flat lists, not theories. Biggest targets: engineering (129c), video_coding_theory (128c), computer_architecture (122c).
     files: seeds/engineering.json (and similar) — add 'term' fields with Holds() pointing at sibling concepts; this also feeds shape diversity (axis 5).

  3. FIX STUCK CORTEX AXIS: data_drivenness (sits at 8)
     rationale: 3 of 5 cortex axes show no variance across 153 Mts — they cannot discriminate good Mts from bad. Either change the scorer's input signal or delete the axis to stop inflating the cortex's 'overall' score.
     files: domains/architecture_assessment.py (score_data_drivenness() — read a SIGNAL that VARIES across Mts, e.g. concept Term-tree presence / shape diversity / intra-Mt connectivity from survey #3 or #5)

